 text+='## Targets, bounds and historical sensitivity\n\nFor fixed pair volumes `T_i=A_i+B_i`, let `s_i=A_i/T_i`, `T=ΣT_i` and `M=ΣT_i(2s_i−1)`. The unbounded tie shift is `(B−A)/(2(A+B)) = −M/(2T)`. Target pair margin `g` requires `(gT−M)/(2T)`. Thus **A+1 pair margin adds0.5 share points before clipping**, not one share point. A+1 margin is `0.01T` net votes; a+1pp A-share transfer gains `0.02T_i` net votes in unit i. All-candidate margin is net divided by the separate final valid-candidate denominator. The +1pp gain column is the unsaturated derivative; `bounded_gain_for_1pp_share` separately clips that proposed local increment at 100%. Counts, share points, margin points and cushions have separate columns.\n\nThe implemented bounded solve finds `δ` such that `ΣT_i[2 clip(s_i+δ,0,1)−1]=gT`. Raw unbounded targets remain visible. Native2024 clipping changes the statewide root; merely clipping a precomputed unbounded answer would miss the tie. Zero-pair units remain present with no-positive-pool status and undefined shares; null pair preferences/pools remain unknown. Already-winning baselines retain signed negative tie shifts, and minimum nonnegative improvement is separate. Impossible targets retain their unbounded values. [Calculator implementation](data/baselines/calculate.py).\n\n'
